# Desktop review evidence

Device: Chromium headless, 1440×900, device scale 1. Existing production server only. No application files or server processes changed.

## Findings

- **Major — English remains the task and the assessed subject in Following a rule.** URL: http://localhost:3417/play/pupil; all eight levels p-1..p-8. `src/games/pupil/levels.ts:8,44,72,113,156,196,242,277` explicitly ask the player to teach English articles, plurals, past-tense spelling, comparatives, verb patterns, count nouns, third-person endings and -ing spelling. The end-card and notebook descriptions return `r.rule` at line 346. Evidence: `047-pupil-misread.png`, `056-pupil-final.png`, `151-later-pupil-end.png`, `156-later-pupil3-end.png`. The philosophy is added in explanatory text; success still depends on correcting English forms. **Fix:** replace the English grammar curriculum with continuation, training, correction and agreement tasks that make rule-following itself the player’s problem; assess and recap those philosophical distinctions.
- **Major — the two final games substitute quizzes for the promised activity.** URLs: http://localhost:3417/play/beetle and /play/hinges, all four sessions. `src/games/choice/ChoiceGame.tsx:59,76–138` implements only choosing a proposition, receiving a reply and proceeding. The box, private diary, ordinary investigation and moving river-bed are static illustrations. Evidence: `160-session-the-beetle.png`, `168-session-the-diary.png`, `175-session-doubt-it.png`, `182-session-the-river-bed.png`, `initial-hinges.png`. **Fix:** make at least the core argument of each game an action with observable consequences: coordinate a public task while hidden box contents change; attempt to maintain/correct diary usage under different criteria; investigate a claim and expose the commitments its checks rely on. Keep multiple-choice reflection after the activity.
- **Major — chosen Notebook composition is not carried through.** URL http://localhost:3417/. Compare `art/ui-v2/a.png` with `001-home.png`. At 1440×900 the built wordmark wraps to two oversized lines, the introduction takes four lines, the hero is a rectangular scenic painting, and the seven game illustrations are mostly below the first viewport. The chosen design gives the compact single-line wordmark, short deck, cut-paper portrait and complete illustrated seven-stop path visual priority. The game screens use large full-scene storybook paintings and pill navigation rather than the chosen lighter editorial collage treatment. Source anchors: `src/app/page.tsx:34,44,47,59`. **Fix:** match the chosen composition and artwork treatment: reduce hero height, use its portrait/collage silhouette, recover the compact title/deck and show the seven illustrated choices together on desktop; carry those typography, paper-edge and illustration rules into games/end cards/reading pages.
- **Minor — the pupil’s “right first time” score is mislabeled.** URL http://localhost:3417/play/pupil, session Teach the pupil. All four final decisions were submitted correctly the first time (`048`, `050`, `052`, `054` screenshots display “Good call”), but `056-pupil-final.png` says “0 of 4 right first time”. `src/games/pupil/PupilGame.tsx:84–85` also requires minimum example-card usage. **Fix:** base “right first time” on the first decision, or explicitly label teaching efficiency separately. Exploring examples should not be reported as answering incorrectly.

## Coverage

`python qa/codex-review-r1/desktop/review.py` completed all seven games, all 23 sessions, all 119 authored rounds. `run.log`: COMPLETE builder/scene/cafe/pupil/family/later/choice and ERRORS []. `storage.json` records 119 completed rounds from visible browser actions. `journey.json` contains 193 URL/body/screenshot observations, none with document horizontal overflow. Every captured image was visually examined in contact sheets 01–13; findings and representative game/end/reading-page screens were also viewed at full size.

All 23 session end cards were observed. The main run captured 22 distinct end cards. `builder-session2-end.png` captures the remaining Two slabs — there! end card after a separate visible-control replay. The optional attempt to open “More from Wittgenstein” afterward timed out because that session has one citation and no such disclosure; this is a review-script assumption, not a site failure. The helper is now conditional.

Wrong-answer paths were used in builder, scene, cafe, pupil, family, beetle and hinges. Reloads preserved wrong/selected answers and progress; individual `wrong-*` and `reload-*` evidence, `reloads.json`, and `supplement.log` record the supplemental cases. All 119 rounds persisted through navigation, populated the notebook, caused the home completion panel to appear, and the notebook's visible Play again link started its first scene session; another reload preserved that replay. Sources, empty notebook and populated notebook were captured.

Session coverage: builder 4 (24 rounds); scene 4 (24); cafe 4 (24); family 4 (19); pupil 3 (8); beetle 2 (10); hinges 2 (10). Total 23 sessions / 119 rounds.

Not covered: physical-device or Safari/Firefox behavior, screen-reader speech output, speech-synthesis audibility, network/offline failures, philosophical quotation verification (assigned to the separate research reviewer), statistical evidence of learning retention.

