## Evidence and limits

- `source-data.json`: the 44 catalog entries read for the quotation/gloss audit.
- `authored-data.json`: evaluated authored content, including all session and round objects, without UI execution.
- `coverage.json`: machine-readable list of all 119 unique round IDs and inspected file locations.
- Normalized PI comparison matched 22 entries immediately; remaining entries were checked for explicitly marked ellipses, OCR, pagination and the one spelling variance above. The other named works were compared section by section through the web tool.
- The English source links are publicly accessible transcriptions/scans of primary books, not publisher-hosted official digital editions. No attempt was made to settle competing scholarly interpretations of private language, rule-following or hinge epistemology.

Not covered: engine behaviour, every possible answer path, runtime/source-bundle parity, historical linguistic frequency claims, empirical effectiveness with learners, or a legal assessment of quotation permissions. Those are not implied by the 44-quotation/119-round content coverage. The coordinator's separate production journey covers runtime use.

